      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "According to the [[credential-scoping]] page, the Anthropic API key is **injected into the spawned child-process environment** \u2014 specifically, it\u0027s injected into the environment of the Ingest agent (and also the Query agent) immediately before that process starts.\n\nThe key detail is that the Hub itself never holds the API key in its own process environment. Instead, a local secrets loader reads the key from a git-ignored \u0060.env\u0060 file at startup and injects it only into the child process environment. This means the Hub\u0027s own process environment is never mutated, so a compromised Hub process cannot leak the credential by inspecting its own environment variables \u2014 the key exists only within the short-lived child process that actually calls the Anthropic API.",
      "input_tokens": 5317,
